}\" part of this formula might not work correctly on large data sets."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["If your data set exceeds the 500 record limit but contains less than 2,000 records, try resetting the limit.","Try simplifying the formula.","Try moving your data to a different data source."],"whyFix":"","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrInvalidName","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Name isn't valid. '{0}' isn't recognized."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Remove or correct the reference to the name that isn't valid."],"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrInvalidArgs-Func","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"The function '{0}' has some invalid arguments."}},"properties":{"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrIncompatibleCtxtVariableTypes","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Incompatible type. We can't evaluate your formula because the context variable types are incompatible with the types of values in other places in your app."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Look at places where you use a context variable and make sure that the type (e.g., text, number, date, record, table) is compatible."],"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrUnknownNamespaceFunction","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"'{0}' is an unknown or unsupported function in namespace '{1}'."}},"properties":{"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrInvalidDot","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"The '.' operator cannot be used on {0} values."}},"properties":{"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrIncompatibleTypesForEquality-Left-Right","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Incompatible types for comparison. These types can't be compared: {0}, {1}."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["You might need to convert the value to be the same type, such as converting a date string (e.g., \"12/31/2018\") to a date value.","If you're comparing records or tables, the field or column types must match exactly."],"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-SuggestRemoteExecutionHint-OpNotSupportedByService","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Delegation warning. The highlighted part of this formula might not work correctly on large data sets. The \"{0}\" operation is not supported by this connector."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["If your data set exceeds the 500 record limit but contains less than 2,000 records, try resetting the limit.","Try simplifying the formula.","Try moving your data to a different data source."],"whyFix":"","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrBadType","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Invalid argument type."}},"properties":{"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrBadType-ExpectedType-ProvidedType","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Invalid argument type ({1}). Expecting a {0} value instead."}},"properties":{"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrBadSchema-ExpectedType","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Invalid argument type. Expecting a {0} value, but of a different schema."}},"properties":{"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-ErrColumnTypeMismatch-ColName-ExpectedType-ActualType","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Incompatible type. The '{0}' column in the data source you're updating expects a '{1}' type and you're using a '{2}' type."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["You might need to convert the value to the same type, such as converting a date string (e.g., \"12/31/2018\") to a date value or a string to a number."],"whyFix":"","level":"High","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"app-SuggestRemoteExecutionHint-OpNotSupportedByColumn","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Delegation warning. The highlighted part of this formula might not work correctly with column \"{0}\" on large data sets."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["If your data set exceeds the 500 record limit but contains less than 2,000 records, try resetting the limit.","Try simplifying the formula.","Try moving your data to a different data source."],"whyFix":"","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"formula"}},{"id":"acc-TabIndexShouldBeDefinedForInteractiveControl","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Missing tab stop"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Set TabIndex to 0 or greater to ensure that interactive elements have a tab stop."],"whyFix":"People who use the keyboard with your app will not be able to access this element without a tab stop.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"acc-AccessibleLabelNeeded","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Missing accessible label"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Edit the accessible label property to describe the item."],"whyFix":"If there's no accessible text, people who can’t see the screen won't understand what’s in images and controls.","level":"Medium","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"accessibility"}},{"id":"app-UnusedVariables","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Unused variable"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Remove the unused variable."],"whyFix":"This variable is declared but is not referenced by any control, so it is not needed.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}},{"id":"app-UnusedMediaResources","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Unused media files"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Remove the unused media file in the Media pane."],"whyFix":"This media file is not referenced by any control formulas so it is not needed. Removing it will improve performance.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}},{"id":"app-CollectDelegatableDataSource","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"The rows retrieved from the data source may not be complete."}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Limit the data collected from the data source by updating the formula \"ClearCollect(colProgrammes, Programmes)\" to include a filtering function, such as 'Filter' or 'Search'."],"whyFix":"Using the 'Collect' function to create a collection directly from a connected data source may not load every row if the data source is too large.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}},{"id":"app-DataSourceDefaultMaxRowsLimit","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Data row limit for non-delegable queries is more than 500"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Update 'Data row limit for non-delegable queries' in the advanced app settings."],"whyFix":"A 'data row limit' more than 500 may result in a slower app when running non-delegable queries, because the app will have to process every row itself, rather than running the query on the server.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}},{"id":"app-CollectingReadOnlyTable","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Collection is initialized but never updated"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Replace the Collect or ClearCollect with a named formula on App.Formulas. For example, MyTable = Filter(source, condition). Named formulas are computed when their inputs change and do not carry the tracking cost of a collection."],"whyFix":"Collections are meant to be updated. Power Apps does extra work to keep track of every collection so that anything depending on it stays in sync when the data changes. When the data never changes after it is set, that tracking work is wasted. A named formula gives the same data without the extra cost.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}},{"id":"app-InefficientDelayLoading","messageStrings":{"issue":{"text":"Inefficient delay loading"}},"properties":{"howToFix":["Use variables, collections, and navigation context to share state across screens instead."],"whyFix":"Controls that reference controls on other screens can slow down app loading and navigation. Doing this may force the app to load the other screens immediately, rather than waiting until the user navigates to that screen.","componentType":"app","primaryCategory":"performance","level":"Medium"}}]}},"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits"}]}